{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>נטשו.</b> Like חבליך, opposite the camp of Assyria." "<b>נטשו</b> like ונטשתה (Exodus 23:11), by way of parable: the ship sinks and the sea casts out the wealth that is in it." "<b>בל.</b> The sailors hold fast their mast, and do not spread a sail — then [one] divides spoil without limit, like אדמת עפר (Daniel 12:2), from the root of בבקר יאכל עד (Genesis 49:27)." "<b>מרבה.</b> Like הרבה איספו פסחים בזזו בז, how much more so others."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {2 "Ibn Ezra reads עד in the Daniel verse as related to the root of Genesis 49:27; the precise grammatical argument is compressed and left as-is.", 3 "The citation appears truncated or elliptical; translated hyper-literally as it stands."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:56:37.024715253Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}